        "title": "Equivalent fractions",
        "text": "Fractional equivalence tells us that $$\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{c}{d}$$ if and only if $$b$$ and $$d$$ are nonzero and $$ad=bc$$.",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "a6dd06fbasicalgvidonemodthree14a-h2",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "a6dd06fbasicalgvidonemodthree14a-h1"
        ],
        "title": "Equivalent fractions",
        "text": "Cross multiply. Here we get \\n $$\\frac{x+2}{x-2}=\\frac{4}{x-2}$$ \\n if and only if $$(x-1)(x-2)=4(x-2)$$.",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "a6dd06fbasicalgvidonemodthree14a-h3",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "a6dd06fbasicalgvidonemodthree14a-h2"
        ],
        "title": "Subtract $$4(x-2)$$ from both sides",
        "text": "$$\\left(x+2\\right) \\left(x-2\\right)-4\\left(x-2\\right)=4(x-2)-4(x-2)=0$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "a6dd06fbasicalgvidonemodthree14a-h4",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "a6dd06fbasicalgvidonemodthree14a-h3"
        ],
        "title": "Factor $$(x-2)$$ on LHS",
        "text": "$$\\left(x+2\\right) \\left(x-2\\right)-4\\left(x-2\\right)=$$ $$\\left(x+2-4\\right) \\left(x-2\\right)=0$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "a6dd06fbasicalgvidonemodthree14a-h5",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "a6dd06fbasicalgvidonemodthree14a-h4"
        ],
        "title": "Simplify",
        "text": "$$\\left(x+2-4\\right) \\left(x-2\\right)=(x-2)(x-2)=\\left(x-2\\right)^2=0$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "a6dd06fbasicalgvidonemodthree14a-h6",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "a6dd06fbasicalgvidonemodthree14a-h5"
        ],
        "title": "Zero product property",
        "text": "$$\\left(x-2\\right)^2$$ is greater than or equal to zero for all $$x.$$ It is equal to zero only when $$x=2$$.",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "a6dd06fbasicalgvidonemodthree14a-h7",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "a6dd06fbasicalgvidonemodthree14a-h6"
        ],
        "title": "Conclusion",
        "text": "Notice that when $$x=2$$, the denominator of the original equation is zero! This is not a valid solution. Therefore, there are no solutions to this equation.",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    }
]